  "hindi": "सुपर्ण पहले उत्पन्न हुआ; तुम उसका पित्त (पित्तरस) थीं। तब असुर-स्त्री ने, युद्ध में जीती जाकर, वनस्पतियों को रूप बना लिया।",
  "english": "The well-winged one (Suparṇa) was born first; you were his gall. Then the Asura-woman, conquered in battle, made the trees (her) form.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "suparṇaḥ is kept as the name/epithet 'well-winged one'; no identification is made. pittam is the literal 'gall/bile'. The last words rūpaṃ cakre vanaspatīn are ambiguous: 'made the trees her form' is a literal rendering; Whitney-type readings differ (assumed shape as trees). The referent of tvam (the herb or the colour addressed) is not stated.",
